            <history xml:id="history_id615736a0">
               <p xml:id="idm44">See introduction to SchW B5:Coll.006.<lb xml:id="idm45"/>The song appears on pp. 48–50. Scheibe has heavily revised and re-translated Schlegel's translation of the French original and has included two new texts to the same original melody. A footnote to the present song explains that 'this translation of the song, <rend xml:id="idm46" fontstyle="italic">Freres et Compagnons de la Ma Maçonnerie etc.</rend>, has been introduced here, because it is authorised, as it were, by its prolonged use. We have, however, added to it the greatly improved translation of the late Schlegel, together with the translation of the sequel to the song as it begins in the original, Freres et Companons de cette Ordre sublime. These three songs are sung according to the present, original French melody.'</p>
            </history>
